{{also|monologué}}
==English==

===Etymology===
[[circa#English|Circa]] 1550, from circa 1500 {{bor|en|frm|monologue}}, modeled on {{m|frm|dialogue}}, ultimately from {{etyl|grc|en}} or via {{der|en|gkm|μονόλογος||speaking alone}}.

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|monolog}} {{qualifier|US|noun}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|drama}} A long [[speech]] by one person in a play; sometimes a [[soliloquy]]; other times spoken to other characters.
# {{lb|en|comedy}} A long series of [[comic]] [[story|stories]] and [[joke]]s as an [[entertainment]].
# A long, uninterrupted utterance that monopolizes a conversation.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|drama}} {{l|en|soliloquy}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|a monopolizing utterance}} {{l|en|dialogue}}

